`k:in=a, b` splits its operand on the comma and trims each option, so the space-prefixed
second option still matches a row; the status neither option names stays out.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: Alpha
status: ready-for-dev
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/beta/index.md --
---
title: Beta
status: done
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/gamma/index.md --
---
title: Gamma
status: cancelled
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where 'status:in=done, ready-for-dev' --output paths
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
plans/alpha/index.md
plans/beta/index.md
-- stderr --
